{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4531","id":4734195651,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGi4Xww","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4531","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4531.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4531.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4531","number":4531,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SF-A29-T05: cover pinned PDB inputs and bounded workspace ZIP imports","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Task: SF-A29-T05.4, SF-A29-T05.5\nRelated: #1146, #1147; follow-up to #4524/#4527\n\n## Change\n\nExtend the binary targets through existing public package APIs.\n\nThe Portable PDB target now includes the repository's unchanged 712-byte .NET runtime MIT document fixture, pinned by SHA-256, Git blob identity and bounded no-follow reads of its retained license/provenance. Authored boundary inputs cover malformed document indices, embedded source size and reserved DEFLATE blocks.\n\nThe ZIP target now exercises actual `readZip`, `importWorkspaceZip` and `writeNewDirectory` against a fixed, bounded in-memory destination. It checks manifest root selection, returned paths, directories, binary/UTF-16 content and final bytes. Handles have no host filesystem authority and enforce child-only names, collisions, overwrite, count, depth and byte ceilings. Traversal, malformed manifests and bounded declared-output amplification are covered.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Exact local commit `fa5c0fef9093a898b243ee8a02992b993b5c66b3`: **42 focused tests passed, zero failures/skips**, including binary targets, workspace imports and PDB seed/boundary cases.\n- A first integration attempt exposed two syntax errors in asynchronous test assertions; those are corrected. The recorded passing run includes the correction.\n- Published tree `896f9233762f4d93de762b1325a4de9ca81c64d3` exactly matches the tested local tree. Its GitHub-created commit has a different ID.\n- Source review covered fixed input authority, path containment, independent output limits, provenance and unexpected-error handling.\n- Required PR core remains the hosted gate; ordinary core does not execute these Node tests.\n\n## Known finding and remaining scope\n\nThe reserved-DEFLATE PDB input currently escapes the symbols package as plain `Error`. Its focused test verifies that the harness reports and retains an **unexpected-error finding**, not a parser conformance pass. A separate minimal symbols error-contract repair follows; the original input and error must remain reproducible.\n\nNo product package files, dependencies, existing claims or Project fields change in this batch. The scalar-only VM guard remains. Host filesystem extraction semantics and native/other-platform qualification are not inferred from the in-memory writer. Both full issues remain open until their remaining qualification is demonstrated.\n","created_at":"2026-10-04T12:03:04Z","updated_at":"2